<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">f_ref</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    ptr_to_member_func_cvref_test<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span>S<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">f_const</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>i = 123\n*pi = 123\nj = 123</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2101\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2101</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++11\n</td>\n<td>the program was ill-formed if <code>T</code> is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/function#Function_type\">function type</a> with <span class=\"t-spar\">cv</span> or <span class=\"t-spar\">ref</span>\n</td>\n<td>the type produced is <code>T</code> in this case\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_pointer\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>is_pointer</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   checks if a type is a pointer type  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_pointer\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>remove_pointer</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   removes a pointer 